<title>UK: PANAMA LAUNCHES INAUGURAL EUROBOND.</title>
<headline>PANAMA LAUNCHES INAUGURAL EUROBOND.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama issued its first-ever international debt offering on Monday, a $500 million five-year Eurobond.</p>
<p>BankBoston Corp was lead manager for the transaction which was priced to yield 175 basis points more than comparable U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>The issue size was double the $250 million mooted when the deal was first announced in January, due to strong demand, dealers said. It was priced at the tighter end of the expected 175-185 b.p. range.</p>
<p>Panama is rated Ba1 by Moody's Investors Service and BB+ by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>In January it was announced the funds would be used to help pay off the nation's external debt.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
